config-connector-extensions patch 0044: mockgcp serves IAM v3 policy bindings.

For iam.gcp.hfl.dev IAMPolicyBinding. Written here:
mockiam/policybindings.go registers the PolicyBindings gRPC server and, as
patch 0030 does for principal access boundary policies (mockgcp has no
generated HTTP gateway for google.iam.v3), adds the REST paths
(/v3/{organizations,folders,projects}/*/locations/*/policyBindings) to the
mux by hand, calling the server's methods. Create, get, list, update
(display name, annotations and condition, with an update mask; the rest is
immutable) and delete; create, update and delete answer a finished
operation. The bound policy must be a principal access boundary policy the
fake holds; the binding's policy kind and policy uid are set from it. The
etag is computed; an update with a stale etag is refused. Not served:
searchTargetPolicyBindings, and ACCESS policies. Upstream candidate: yes.
Numbered: it edits mockiam/service.go after 0006, 0007, 0010 and 0030.

diff --git a/mockgcp/mockiam/service.go b/mockgcp/mockiam/service.go
